Subject: [PATCH 081/123] installer: SERVICEAUTOSTART flag + document
 silent-install switches
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- ProductBody.wxi: new public property SERVICEAUTOSTART (default 1).
  0 = service installed as Manual and left stopped after install, via a
  deferred SetServiceDemandStart action (sc config start= demand + sc
  stop, Return=ignore) scheduled After="StartServices". WiX's
  ServiceInstall/@Start is an enum, so the flip happens post-start
  instead of duplicating components. Silent install itself needs no new
  machinery — msiexec /quiet already works with the existing UI-less
  sequence.
- Document the full switch set (quiet, AUTOSTART, SERVICEAUTOSTART,
  KEEP_CONFIG, INSTALLFOLDER, /L*v logging, 0/3010 exit codes) in the
  root README, all 12 translated READMEs, installer/README.md and
  installer/DEPLOYMENT.md; DEPLOYMENT.md also corrected for the
  nonexistent CONFIGFILE property, wrong service name and log path.
- Validated by building all 4 brand MSIs via
  installer/wix/build_msi_linux.sh (Docker + wine WiX).

Fork adaptation: the fork's READMEs are kept (the switches are documented
in installer/README.md and installer/DEPLOYMENT.md); SetServiceDemandStart
and DEPLOYMENT.md target the SCM name $(var.ExeName) ("NimbusBackup", see
ServiceInstall), not $(var.ServiceExeName): with the latter, sc config hit a
service that does not exist and SERVICEAUTOSTART=0 did nothing.

